{
  "assessment": "The diff introduces a new rate-limiting `Budget` class to control hourly retry quotas. It tracks spent counts in a dictionary keyed by window index, with a hard limit of three retries per window. However, the window calculation logic is broken, causing all events to collide into a single bucket and permanently exhaust the budget after just three attempts.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "Identical keys (e.g., `0 0`), regardless of input timestamps",
      "at": "retryd/budget.py, Budget.window_key",
      "call": "python -c \"from retryd.budget import Budget; b=Budget(1609459200); print(b.window_key(1609459300), b.window_key(1609462800))\"",
      "defect": "`Budget.window_key` completely ignores its `ts` argument and computes the key solely from `self.started_at`. This buckets every retry event into a single window, so after `PER_WINDOW` (3) retries are spent, `has_room` permanently returns `False` for all subsequent timestamps.",
      "expected": "Two distinct integer values corresponding to different hourly windows based on the input timestamps"
    }
  ]
}
